# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/


# Added by cargo

/target

# Zola site build output and the syntax-highlighting stylesheets Zola regenerates
# into `static/` on every build. Both are derived from `site/` and are rebuilt by
# the deployment workflow, so neither belongs in the repository.
/site/public/
/site/static/giallo-*.css
# Generated by `just site-verify` from the documentation site's code blocks.
/tests/site_examples.rs

# ── Internal notes, feature specifications and third-party sources ─────────────

# Architecture notes (not published): the D/R-numbered decisions and risks, and
# ROADMAP.md, the spec of specs — every open item names its feature specification.
#
# The third-party corpus — regulations, standards, validation artefacts, laws —
# lives at `concepts/reference/` and is covered by this line: copyrighted or
# reciprocally licensed, indexed with retrieval URLs in `concepts/REFERENCES.md`
# and rebuilt with `just references`, so it never needs to be committed.
/concepts/

# This project's own feature specifications, and the Spec Kit machinery that
# produces them: one `specs/NNN-slug/` per ROADMAP item (spec, plan, research,
# tasks), `.specify/memory/constitution.md`, and the `/speckit-*` skills. Same
# rule as `concepts/` — internal, and the published tree may not cite a path its
# reader does not have; `just concepts-check` fails on one that does.
#
# Until 2026-10-09 `specs/` held the third-party corpus now under
# `concepts/reference/`; a stale copy is ignored by the same line.
/specs/
/.specify/
/.claude/
